    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0294" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg270"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Harvey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 132.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 262, of the 28th of
                    February, has been received, and has been read with much interest. The course of
                    events subsequent to its date serves to confirm the correctness of the political
                    intelligence which you have communicated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
